states: triaging -> planning -> investigating -> synthesizing -> proposing
trajectory: d73a27b8-0f1c-4e43-9440-92645668a75e
triage judged: investigate (low confidence, suspects unknown)
  A critical alert on the user-facing edge service cannot be dismissed, and no open incident could account for it. The single seed gives no signal about which downstream dependency or failure mode is responsible.
investigation: 2 round(s), 8 dispatch(es), 24 step(s)

=== PROPOSAL ===
  ABSTAINED - no permitted action fits the evidence
  if wrong    : This abstention is wrong if the service is genuinely frozen and every minute of delay is lost availability at the front door. The observation that would overturn it is narrow and cheap: pod phase Running with restartCount stable at its creation value for nginx-thrift, plus a namespace-scoped Loki query that still returns zero lines for that pod while returning lines for its peers. That combination would meet the restart precondition and I would propose restart_service on nginx-web-server immediately. Conversely, a climbing restartCount, a Pending/CrashLoopBackOff phase, or logs appearing under a broader selector would each confirm the abstention and redirect the investigation.
  rests on    : tr_b42ca415bd08, tr_bdff52fbd51f, tr_77d8e6acee83, tr_28928cb4f5ae, tr_71f8714f5626
  execution   : not executed - a proposal is a claim, never the change (ADR-0028 §1)

context: 27937 pushed / 1581 pulled (pull rate 0.0536), 2 section(s) dropped

=== VERDICT ===
  fault class : process_freeze
  fix class   : restart
  confidence  : low
  evidence    : tr_77d8e6acee83, tr_b42ca415bd08, tr_71f8714f5626, tr_bdff52fbd51f, tr_28928cb4f5ae, tr_e44cb5f7f0bc
  root cause  : The front-door service nginx-web-server stopped doing work while remaining reachable: across the full ~30-minute window spanning onset it emitted no access or error log lines [tr_b42ca415bd08] and not a single span [tr_77d8e6acee83], which is anomalous for an edge proxy that normally logs every request. No change landed between its creation burst and onset to explain a content-level regression [tr_71f8714f5626], and downstream compose-post-service is equally silent [tr_bdff52fbd51f] because nothing is being forwarded to it. Total silence from the alerting entry service with no error signal anywhere is the signature of a stopped process whose socket still accepts, leaving callers to hang to their deadlines. Confidence is low: every metric dispatch returned an unavailable series rather than a measurement [tr_28928cb4f5ae][tr_e44cb5f7f0bc][tr_5c01829f25f9], and both log queries used pod-name regexes that could themselves have missed the pods.
  OPEN        : Pod status and restart counts were never retrieved for nginx-thrift or compose-post-service; a crash-loop or never-ready pod looks identical to a freeze from these dispatches.
  OPEN        : Both Loki queries used pod-name regexes rather than a namespace label and returned an inconsistent truncation flag [tr_b42ca415bd08][tr_bdff52fbd51f], so the zero-match may be a selector miss rather than genuine silence.
  OPEN        : No caller-side evidence was gathered: whether clients hang to deadline or receive immediate errors is the distinction the verdict turns on, and it is unestablished.

